ntdll: process exit returns to boot with the full Windows status
(docs/design/wine-unix.md, section 8, "Process exit (M3)"; abi.md v5,
"Process exit").

Why: Wine ends the host process with the status cut to an exit code
(get_unix_exit_code, thread.c L89-94: a nonzero status with a zero low byte
becomes 1, and _exit keeps only the low 8 bits). The Unix side is one
instance in the JS host, which needs the full status, and boot's promise
must resolve rather than end the runtime.

- exit_process (thread.c L1520-1524) first calls tw_process_exit(status)
  (native/wine/src/boot.c), before get_unix_exit_code. It records the
  status and longjmps to boot, which resets env.depth to 0 and returns the
  status. The longjmp unwinds the translated frames on the wasm stack as a
  wasm exception. exit_process is NtTerminateProcess's end for the current
  process once RtlExitUserProcess's first NtTerminateProcess(0, status) has
  set process_exiting (process.c L980-981), and exit_thread's for the last
  thread (thread.c L1501).
- NtTerminateProcess calls it too, before its own abort_process call
  (process.c L982): a process that ends itself without that first call, as
  TerminateProcess(GetCurrentProcess(), status) does.
- abort_process (thread.c L1485-1488) keeps its _exit. Its other caller is
  abort_thread for the last thread (thread.c L1477), Wine's end for a
  server protocol error (server.c L163, L174), a lost server pipe (L238,
  L267, L977, L1032), a killed thread (L361) and SIGQUIT
  (signal_x86_64.c L2612-2613). Those reject boot's promise with the cut
  status.

Line numbers are wine-11.0's, in dlls/ntdll/unix/.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
@@ -73,6 +73,11 @@
 
 WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(process);
 
+#ifdef __wasm64__
+/* Tempwind's process exit (wine-unix.md, section 8), as in thread.c. */
+extern void DECLSPEC_NORETURN tw_process_exit( int status );
+#endif
+
 
 static ULONG execute_flags = MEM_EXECUTE_OPTION_DISABLE;
 
@@ -984,7 +989,14 @@
     {
         if (!handle) process_exiting = TRUE;
         else if (process_exiting) exit_process( exit_code );
-        else abort_process( exit_code );
+        else
+        {
+#ifdef __wasm64__
+            /* the full status; abort_thread's abort_process keeps its _exit */
+            tw_process_exit( exit_code );
+#endif
+            abort_process( exit_code );
+        }
     }
     return ret;
 }
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
@@ -86,6 +86,12 @@
 
 static LONG nb_threads = 1;
 
+#ifdef __wasm64__
+/* Tempwind's process exit (wine-unix.md, section 8): records the full
+ * Windows status and longjmps to boot, which returns it (boot.c). */
+extern void DECLSPEC_NORETURN tw_process_exit( int status );
+#endif
+
 static inline int get_unix_exit_code( NTSTATUS status )
 {
     /* prevent a nonzero exit code to end up truncated to zero in unix */
@@ -1519,6 +1525,9 @@
  */
 void exit_process( int status )
 {
+#ifdef __wasm64__
+    tw_process_exit( status );  /* the full status, before get_unix_exit_code cuts it */
+#endif
     pthread_sigmask( SIG_BLOCK, &server_block_set, NULL );
     process_exit_wrapper( get_unix_exit_code( status ));
 }
